End-to-End Token Exchange Validation with AgentCore Gateway and Auth0

Objective
We wanted to test whether Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Gateway can integrate with an external identity provider (Auth0) to perform OAuth token exchange and issue a scoped-down token that is used to securely call a downstream tool/API.

The goal was to confirm that:
- An incoming token can be intercepted
- That token can be exchanged through Auth0
- A new token with reduced permissions can be issued
- The downstream tool can execute successfully using the scoped token

