Conclusion

We successfully validated an end-to-end OAuth token exchange flow between Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Gateway and Auth0.

The interceptor Lambda exchanged the incoming token through Auth0 and received a scoped-down token targeting the Addition Tool API. The gateway then completed the tool invocation using that token, and the tool executed successfully.

By decoding both tokens, we confirmed that the exchanged token had a different audience and a reduced scope, proving that token downscoping and secure downstream API access works correctly in this architecture.
